"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data, with a focus on leveraging AI. The project kicked off on June 15th with a $500,000 budget for phase one, led by Sarah Tan. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms. The team expanded to include specialists in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with new members joining in September. Ideas for enhancing data visualization tools were solicited by July 20th. The project moved from design to development, led by Omar Jensen, and successfully reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a tested secure file sharing prototype. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was requested by the end of November. The project is now nearing its final stages, with all tasks expected to be completed according to the agreed timeline."
